 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 489 of the laws of 2004 amending the tax law relating\nto the mortgage recording tax in the county of Fulton, in relation to the\neffectiveness of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S6761",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6761-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 489 of 2004",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6761\n\nSPONSOR: WALCZYK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 489 of the laws of 2004 amending the tax law\nrelating to the mortgage recording tax in the county of Fulton, in\nrelation to the effectiveness of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nExtends authorization of the county of Fulton to impose a county record-\ning tax on obligation secured by a mortgage on real property.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Section 2 of chapter 489 of the laws of 2004 amending the\ntax law relating to authorizing the county of Herkimer to impose a coun-\nty recording tax on obligation secured by a mortgage on real property,\nin relation to extending the effectiveness thereof as amended by section\n1 of item C of subpart E of part XXX of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020,\nis amended.\n\nSection 2 - Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe county of Fulton has requested this legislation to extend their\nauthority to impose a mortgage recording tax in the amount of twenty-\nfive cents for each one hundred dollars, until December 1, 2025. The\nCounty of Fulton is faced with continuing fiscal pressure in the fore-\nseeable future, and wishes to minimize the burden on local property\ntaxpayers; and because of said requirements and others, an extension of\nthe county mortgage recording tax is needed. This was requested by the\nFulton County Board of Supervisors.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
